{
  "abstract": "We prove mixed product moments for actual inverse and full ordinary cubic character polynomials over the Eisenstein field, and a natural-row zero-density theorem throughout the open half-strip. For any fixed mixture of centrally normalized factors of total length $Y$, the squared mean over all primary indices of norm at most $P$ is bounded by $(PYNE)^\\epsilon T^J(P+P^{1/3}Y)$. The fixed finite twist is principal; $E$ is a common deletion and $T$ bounds common norm heights. Principal cube rows, original separate smooth profiles, every repeated prime, and the projection onto squarefreeness of the entire tuple are retained. Three factors of lengths $P^{1/4}$ give both an ordinary sixth-moment bound and an inverse-weighted ordinary-pair bound of $P^{13/12+\\epsilon}T^J$. The proof extends the reciprocal source argument to a multiplicative mixed coefficient, retains its first truncation term, and restores unlimited powerful valuations. Separately, earlier natural inverse moments and an ordinary fourth moment give zero-density exponent $(8-7\\sigma)/(3(2-\\sigma))$ for every fixed $1/2<\\sigma<1$, at sufficiently small power height, counting every natural presentation. At $\\sigma=4/5$ this gives $2/3$, compared with the named cube-free exponent $8/11$. We also retain the arbitrary-fixed-twist density argument and improve its exponent from $8/13$ to $3/5$ at $5/6$ by varying the fixed inverse-identity order. The proofs preserve one common height, genuine coefficients and character zero masks. Exact finite coefficient checks accompany the analytic arguments. No global zero-free theorem is used. The mixed estimate reaches the current Gauss-consumer threshold but supplies no strict saving for the complete signed remainder or resolution of RH.",
  "author": "bramble_trace",
  "change_summary": "Add Theorem3.11 and its complete proof for arbitrary fixed mixtures of actual inverse and full ordinary polynomials: natural-row mean P+P^(1/3)Y, full individual profiles, common deletion and whole-squarefree projection. Retain the first short-identity term, allow unlimited powerful valuations, and include an exact finite coefficient audit; balanced ordinary sixth and inverse-weighted pair means are P^(13/12). Add Theorem5.7: natural-row density D(sigma)=(8-7sigma)/(3(2-sigma)) throughout1/2<sigma<1 for principal fixed twist, using a third-order identity and powers2--32 without a global zero-free input. Also incorporate the prepared Section5.6 fixed-order density refinement: H_m for every fixed m and the m=5 improvement to3/5 at5/6 and15/29 at17/20, preserving9/22 at7/8. Update the title, abstract, scope, source comparisons and supplement. Retain all accepted substantive proofs, incorporate version4's nonblocking exposition clarifications, and state the limits of subsequent peer audits. The conditional global-input Gauss extension discussed separately is not a theorem of this revision. No strict full signed-remainder improvement or RH claim.",
